pain and suffering.

00:10:13.261 --> 00:10:15.140
- In the end, like, what
would your advice be

00:10:15.140 --> 00:10:17.135
to that 16 year old kid
who's staring in the mirror,

00:10:17.135 --> 00:10:19.235
does not like what he sees,

00:10:19.235 --> 00:10:22.681
but is still running from adversity?

00:10:22.681 --> 00:10:24.279
- Well my biggest advice to him is that,

00:10:24.279 --> 00:10:26.489
first of all, he won't
like what I say to him.

00:10:26.489 --> 00:10:28.885
Because I'm going to say the
exact opposite of what the world,

00:10:28.885 --> 00:10:30.442
today's world is saying.

00:10:30.442 --> 00:10:32.468
So we read a bunch of books nowadays.

00:10:32.468 --> 00:10:36.635
As humans, we want to find
out how to be someone else.

00:10:37.963 --> 00:10:41.286
What we don't do, we don't go inside.

00:10:41.286 --> 00:10:43.253
So literally turn yourself inside out.

00:10:43.253 --> 00:10:45.489
Read the book that's;
like we're writing a book

00:10:45.489 --> 00:10:48.638
every day of our lives, but
we never read that book.

00:10:48.638 --> 00:10:50.250
So what I would challenge this young man,

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:51.865
or young woman to do,

00:10:51.865 --> 00:10:53.689
is you have to look inside of yourself

00:10:53.689 --> 00:10:54.912
to see what you really want.

00:10:54.912 --> 00:10:56.523
What are you passionate about?

00:10:56.523 --> 00:10:59.060
We use these words and
these little phrases of

00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:01.605
only the strong survive,
and all this other crap.

00:11:01.605 --> 00:11:04.002
They're all just (expletive) words.

00:11:04.002 --> 00:11:06.418
I get so tired of hearing
people just talking.

00:11:06.418 --> 00:11:10.328
Like right now, someone might
think Doggin's just talking.

00:11:10.328 --> 00:11:11.278
You don't know me.

00:11:11.278 --> 00:11:13.111
So when I speak I speak from passion,

00:11:13.111 --> 00:11:16.165
I speak from experience,
I speak from suffering.

00:11:16.165 --> 00:11:18.208
I would have to tell
this young man or woman

00:11:18.208 --> 00:11:20.018
that the only way, I believe;

00:11:20.018 --> 00:11:22.269
and this is my experience in life.

00:11:22.269 --> 00:11:25.523
The only way you're ever
going to get to the other side

00:11:25.523 --> 00:11:29.690
of this journey, is you
have got to suffer to grow.

00:11:30.968 --> 00:11:32.637
To grow, you must suffer.

00:11:32.637 --> 00:11:36.646
And some people get it,
and some people won't.

00:11:36.646 --> 00:11:38.325
But they have to see
what their journey is,

00:11:38.325 --> 00:11:39.158
to start their journey.

00:11:39.158 --> 00:11:41.307
Several people live to be 100 years old,

00:11:41.307 --> 00:11:43.179
and they have great lives,
and they have great kids.

00:11:43.179 --> 00:11:45.412
Their kids go to college,
and all sort of other stuff.

00:11:45.412 --> 00:11:47.525
But somewhere in their life,

00:11:47.525 --> 00:11:50.874
there was a point where
they had a decision to make.

00:11:50.874 --> 00:11:53.184
They can go left or right on this path.

00:11:53.184 --> 00:11:57.201
Left was the easy route,
right was the hard route.

00:11:57.201 --> 00:11:59.409
A lot of people take the easy route.

00:11:59.409 --> 00:12:01.348
And they had a good life that way,

00:12:01.348 --> 00:12:04.114
but the better life was
going to the right side.

00:12:04.114 --> 00:12:05.413
And you may have 20 years

00:12:05.413 --> 00:12:07.705
of pain and suffering to get past it,

00:12:07.705 --> 00:12:11.530
but a lot of us die never
truly starting our journey.

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:13.582
And I would tell this young person,

00:12:13.582 --> 00:12:14.798
you've got to start your journey.

00:12:14.798 --> 00:12:18.455
It may suck, but it will
come out the other side

00:12:18.455 --> 00:12:19.691
where you're coasting.

00:12:19.691 --> 00:12:22.332
- If you find your passion,

00:12:22.332 --> 00:12:24.233
you're going to have
this tremendous energy,

00:12:24.233 --> 00:12:26.437
a sustainable energy.

00:12:26.437 --> 00:12:29.621
But momentum requires you
always do the next thing

00:12:29.621 --> 00:12:31.618
to keep the momentum going.

00:12:31.618 --> 00:12:36.516
And the reason you get
yourself in a passionate place,

00:12:36.516 --> 00:12:38.154
is so that you change your life.

00:12:38.154 --> 00:12:39.560
And the only thing that changes your life

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:41.366
is making a decision.

00:12:41.366 --> 00:12:44.627
So while you're in this passionate state,

00:12:44.627 --> 00:12:47.007
that's when you make decisions.

00:12:47.007 --> 00:12:50.100
You don't make decisions when you're like,

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:53.525
I don't know, what do you
think, alright let's decide.

00:12:53.525 --> 00:12:56.533
If you make a decision in
a state without momentum,

00:12:56.533 --> 00:12:58.271
if you make a decision from a place

00:12:58.271 --> 00:12:59.868
where there's no passion,

00:12:59.868 --> 00:13:01.281
you are not going to get momentum.

00:13:01.281 --> 00:13:02.838
It'll kill momentum.

00:13:02.838 --> 00:13:05.588
It's decide, commit, and resolve.

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:10.042
Some of you,

00:13:10.042 --> 00:13:12.766
in the past you've gotten momentum.

00:13:12.766 --> 00:13:14.254
You've gotten passionate.

00:13:14.254 --> 00:13:16.497
You've even made a decision,

00:13:16.497 --> 00:13:19.247
but a decision is the first step.

00:13:20.630 --> 00:13:22.544
Decision is like a war.

00:13:22.544 --> 00:13:23.915
I got to do this or that.

00:13:23.915 --> 00:13:26.401
Alright I'm going to make myself do this.

00:13:26.401 --> 00:13:30.846
But commitment is when you
now, after you've decided

00:13:30.846 --> 00:13:33.277
you commit to do this for the long term.

00:13:33.277 --> 00:13:37.592
Whether it's hard or easy doesn't
matter, you're doing this.

00:13:37.592 --> 00:13:39.495
It takes it from this moment,

00:13:39.495 --> 00:13:41.202
and it carries it into the future,

00:13:41.202 --> 00:13:43.445
even when things are difficult.

00:13:43.445 --> 00:13:46.028
And the third state is resolve.

00:13:47.134 --> 00:13:49.134
Resolve means it's done.

00:13:51.125 --> 00:13:52.633
It's like, it doesn't
even if you take action,

00:13:52.633 --> 00:13:56.030
it's done inside you,
so it's done out there.

00:13:56.030 --> 00:13:57.961
There's no question whatsoever.

00:13:57.961 --> 00:13:59.711
Then once you decide,

00:14:00.796 --> 00:14:02.825
the only way the
commitment, and the energy,

00:14:02.825 --> 00:14:04.227
and the momentum continues,

00:14:04.227 --> 00:14:07.838
is if you take immediate,
massive, what my friends?

00:14:07.838 --> 00:14:08.921
Massive what?

00:14:09.814 --> 00:14:13.981
Write down in your notes,
massive action is the cure all.

00:14:15.442 --> 00:14:18.025
Massive action is the cure all.

00:14:18.863 --> 00:14:21.229
If you're having a difficult
time with something,

00:14:21.229 --> 00:14:23.676
your relationship isn't
where you want it to be,

00:14:23.676 --> 00:14:25.572
your finances are not
where you want to be,

00:14:25.572 --> 00:14:27.081
your body's not where you want to be,

00:14:27.081 --> 00:14:28.968
your business is not
where you want it to be.

00:14:28.968 --> 00:14:31.049
You need to take massive action.

00:14:31.049 --> 00:14:32.738
And if that doesn't
work, try something else.

00:14:32.738 --> 00:14:34.280
If that doesn't work, try something else.

00:14:34.280 --> 00:14:36.789
Keep going with massive action,

00:14:36.789 --> 00:14:38.403
and you will find the way

00:14:38.403 --> 00:14:40.920
because it will give you momentum.

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:43.667
- How do we get people
to become success seekers

00:14:43.667 --> 00:14:46.844
rather than failure avoiders?

00:14:46.844 --> 00:14:48.954
First day of introductory
psychology class,

00:14:48.954 --> 00:14:51.260
I teach two classes of 600 students.

00:14:51.260 --> 00:14:52.615
Maybe some of you have been in that class.

00:14:52.615 --> 00:14:55.419
And remember, the first day I say,

00:14:55.419 --> 00:14:58.973
how many are here to avoid failure?

00:14:58.973 --> 00:15:01.752
And 80% raise their hand.

00:15:01.752 --> 00:15:03.906
And I say, well thanks for coming.

00:15:03.906 --> 00:15:08.093
I know you're motivated, but
you're not happy campers.

00:15:08.093 --> 00:15:11.629
You probably told your
friends I got to go to class,

00:15:11.629 --> 00:15:13.804
it's a requirement.

00:15:13.804 --> 00:15:17.573
Not, I get to go to class,
it's an opportunity.

00:15:17.573 --> 00:15:20.215
You probably woke up to an alarm clock,

00:15:20.215 --> 00:15:22.298
not an opportunity clock.

00:15:23.225 --> 00:15:24.870
And it's all in how you see it.

00:15:24.870 --> 00:15:26.780
Really, it's all in how you see it.

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:28.003
It's your paradigm.

00:15:28.003 --> 00:15:29.995
It's how you communicate to others,

00:15:29.995 --> 00:15:33.316
and how you communicate to yourself.

00:15:33.316 --> 00:15:37.663
So Ellen Langer said in
her book Mindfulness.

00:15:37.663 --> 00:15:39.637
She said, and psychologists know,

00:15:39.637 --> 00:15:43.804
when you perceive choice,
you perceive motivation.

00:15:44.687 --> 00:15:46.005
You're more motivated.

00:15:46.005 --> 00:15:49.371
So the deal is, for yourself,
sit back and reflect.

00:15:49.371 --> 00:15:52.022
Be mindful of the choices you have.

00:15:52.022 --> 00:15:54.505
And talk about being a success seeker,

00:15:54.505 --> 00:15:56.021
rather than a failure avoider.

00:15:56.021 --> 00:15:58.697
It's all how you talk, how
you communicate to yourself,

00:15:58.697 --> 00:15:59.864
and to others.

